# Database Schema Documentation

This document provides a comprehensive specification of the relational database schema for the **File Ingestion Engine**, constructed using **SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM** models with **Alembic** versioned migrations.

---

## 1. Architectural Overview & Design Patterns

The database architecture is designed for high-performance file ingestion, deduplication, virtual directory mapping, multi-provider cloud background synchronization, and security auditing.

```
                      +-------------------+
                      |       users       |
                      +---------+---------+
                                |
       +------------------------+------------------------+-----------------------+
       | 1:N                    | 1:N                    | 1:N                   | 1:N
       v                        v                        v                       v
+--------------+         +--------------+         +--------------+        +----------------------+
|  audit_logs  |         |   datasets   |         |   folders    |        | async_ingestion_jobs |
+--------------+         +------+-------+         +------+-------+        +----------+-----------+
                                |                        |                           |
                                | 1:N                    | 1:N                       | N:1 (SET NULL)
                                v                        v                           |
                         +--------------------------------------+                    |
                         |    dataset_folder_files_mapping      |                    |
                         +-------------------+------------------+                    |
                                             |                                       |
                                             | N:1                                   |
                                             v                                       v
                                    +------------------+                    +------------------+
                                    |  uploaded_files  |<-------------------|  uploaded_files  |
                                    +--------+---------+  1:N (master_hash) +------------------+
                                             |
                                             | 1:N (master_hash)
                                             v
                                 +-----------------------+
                                 | provider_hash_mappings|
                                 +-----------------------+
```

### Key Architectural Concepts:
1. **Global Content Deduplication (`uploaded_files.master_hash`)**: Files uploaded to the system are stored physically only once based on their SHA-256 checksum (`master_hash`). Subsequent uploads of identical content immediately short-circuit without consuming additional disk space.
2. **Virtual Folder & Dataset Hierarchy (`folders` & `dataset_folder_files_mapping`)**: Physical storage paths (`physical_path`) are completely decoupled from logical user presentation. Users can create virtual nested folder structures (`folders.parent_id`) and map files into multiple datasets via junction records (`dataset_folder_files_mapping`).
3. **Cloud & Multi-Provider Hash Rosetta Stone (`provider_hash_mappings`)**: Translates provider-native hashes (e.g. Google Drive `md5Checksum`, OneDrive/SharePoint `quickXorHash`) to the server's canonical `master_hash`, allowing instant zero-download deduplication across external cloud platforms.
4. **Asynchronous Ingestion Ledger (`async_ingestion_jobs`)**: Tracks stateful background ingestion tasks (e.g., FTP pull, Google Drive sync, SharePoint ingestion) with byte-level progress reporting and resumable Range requests.
5. **Immutable Audit Logging (`audit_logs`)**: Captures HTTP request diagnostics, execution duration, action metrics, client IP, user agent, and unique request identifiers.

